## Acknowledgements

LinCa builds on the feature-caching line of work, and this repository builds on the open-source releases that made the experiments possible:

  * FreqCa (arXiv:2510.08669) — the frequency-decomposition cache that LinCa generalises, replacing its fixed FFT/DCT split with a learned invertible one. The cache bookkeeping in `cache_functions/` keeps FreqCa's interface, and `cache_utils.py` stays in every tree as the baseline path.
  * TaylorSeer (ICCV 2025) — Taylor-expansion feature forecasting, our closest baseline and the origin of the video-model cache scaffolding in the HunyuanVideo and Wan2.1 trees.
  * Backbones: FLUX (Black Forest Labs), Qwen-Image and Qwen-Image-Edit (Alibaba), HunyuanVideo (Tencent), Wan2.1 (Alibaba).
  * Evaluation: VBench, ImageReward, GEdit-Bench.

