# Mitigating Over-Refusal in Aligned Large Language Models via Inference-Time Activation Energy

LLMs refuse you too much? This fix dials up the "helpfulness" dial at inference.

Published 3/4/2026 by Eric Hanchen Jiang, Weixuan Ou, Run Liu, Shengyuan Pang, Guancheng Wan, Ranjie Duan, Wei Dong and 4 more...

## Overview

  * Large language models trained to refuse harmful requests sometimes refuse legitimate, safe requests too
  * This over-refusal problem reduces usefulness while keeping safety features intact
  * Researchers developed an energy-based steering technique to reduce false refusals
  * The method works by analyzing internal neural activations during refusal decisions
  * The approach collects data from model responses, identifies refusal patterns, and uses that information to guide the model toward appropriate answers
  * Early results show the technique reduces false refusals while maintaining safety guardrails

## Plain English Explanation
