L241: Note
L242: 
L243: FLOPs speedup and wall-clock speedup are different quantities. Latency varies with GPU, attention kernels, resolution, batch size, and software versions. Always compare with a baseline measured in the same environment.
L244: ## 🛠 Installation
L245: 
L246:     git clone https://github.com/Tammytcl/FreqCa.git
L247:     cd FreqCa
L248: 
L249: Python 3.10 or 3.11 and a CUDA-capable PyTorch environment are recommended. Because the two model families use different upstream inference stacks, separate environments are the safest setup.
L250: 
L251: ### FLUX environment
L252: 
L253:     conda create -n freqca-flux python=3.10 -y
L254:     conda activate freqca-flux
L255:     pip install -e "./flux[torch]"
L256: ### Qwen-Image environment
L257: 
L258:     conda create -n freqca-qwen python=3.10 -y
L259:     conda activate freqca-qwen
L260:     pip install -r qwen_image/requirements.txt
L261: 
L262: Weights are downloaded from Hugging Face on first use. For gated checkpoints, accept the model terms and authenticate with:
L263: 
L264:     hf auth login
L265: 
L266: ## ⚡ FreqCa-FLUX
L267: 
L268: FreqCa supports FLUX.1-dev, FLUX.1-schnell, FLUX.1-Kontext-dev, and FLUX.1-Fill-dev. The paper uses DCT decomposition for FLUX models.

